1
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,280
It's okay, no need to change shoes.

2
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:39,959
Come in.

3
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:44,599
Why hasn't my mom come back yet?

4
00:01:47,879 --> 00:01:48,840
You've been doing

5
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,680
pretty well on that case lately.

6
00:01:50,359 --> 00:01:51,400
It's my mom.

7
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:52,599
What would you like to drink?

8
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:53,560
I'll get it for you.

9
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:55,760
What's wrong?

10
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:56,799
No, it's not...

11
00:02:05,799 --> 00:02:06,879
Come in, please.

12
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:09,639
It's so hard

13
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:10,840
to see you these days.

14
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,800
Why are you hiding?

15
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,360
Listen to what they're talking about.

16
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,560
Maybe you'll find the answer you're looking for.

17
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:18,680
You're really shuttling back and forth every day?

18
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:20,680
It's just a temporary reassignment.

19
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:22,319
It'll be over in two months.

20
00:02:22,319 --> 00:02:22,800
Come on.

21
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,159
Have a seat.

22
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,599
Have you told Zhou Yang yet?

23
00:02:27,479 --> 00:02:28,400
I haven't told him yet.

24
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,840
Then why do you come home on time every day?

25
00:02:32,319 --> 00:02:33,280
What do you want to do?

26
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:34,280
Are you running for

27
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:35,840
the title of "Good Mother of China"?

28
00:02:36,199 --> 00:02:37,280
No.

29
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:38,960
It's just that home is here.

30
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,039
I think

31
00:02:42,039 --> 00:02:43,039
your Zhou Yang

32
00:02:43,039 --> 00:02:44,639
is quite reliable.

33
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:47,240
With Yanyan's situation,

34
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:48,639
I can let go.

35
00:02:48,879 --> 00:02:50,159
What do you have to worry about?

36
00:02:51,199 --> 00:02:51,879
What's wrong?

37
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,319
Are you afraid Zhou Yang will learn bad habits,

38
00:02:53,639 --> 00:02:55,400
or that he can't take care of himself?

39
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:56,560
No.

40
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,800
Actually, it's not that I don't trust Zhou Yang.

41
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,120
During this period,

42
00:03:06,759 --> 00:03:07,840
I spend two hours every day

43
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:08,960
in the car.

44
00:03:09,759 --> 00:03:11,159
When I'm spacing out, I think,

45
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,080
what am I doing?

46
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,120
Why am I exhausting myself

47
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:15,000
like this every day?

48
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:16,919
Later,

49
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:20,159
I figured it out.

50
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:21,639
You know,

51
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:24,000
I finally returned to the workplace.

52
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,520
If I say I'm not scared

53
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,479
or confused,

54
00:03:26,479 --> 00:03:27,599
that would be a lie.

55
00:03:29,439 --> 00:03:30,319
But,

56
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,120
the one

57
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,639
who keeps me going

58
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,759
is Zhou Yang.

59
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,879
Every day when I come home,

60
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,439
as long as I see him,

61
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,120
I feel

62
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,439
completely refreshed.

63
00:03:46,159 --> 00:03:47,240
And the next day,

64
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,360
I'm ready to

65
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,319
keep pushing.

66
00:03:50,319 --> 00:03:51,599
So,

67
00:03:53,639 --> 00:03:55,000
it's not that I don't trust Zhou Yang,

68
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:56,800
it's just that

69
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,599
I can't live without him.

70
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,520
I see.

71
00:04:01,439 --> 00:04:04,560
You're like an electric car,

72
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:06,800
and you need to go home to recharge every day.

73
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:09,240
Otherwise, you won't have the energy to work the next day.

74
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:12,120
Your metaphor...

75
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:13,520
Actually,

76
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,439
it's quite accurate.

77
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,480
What kind of metaphor is that?

78
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:20,560
If you put it that way,

79
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,920
I'm like a gasoline car.

80
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,560
Every day, when I'm outside,

81
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,000
I can fully rev up the engine.

82
00:04:27,199 --> 00:04:28,360
But that's not quite right.

83
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,480
I should be a hybrid.

84
00:04:32,279 --> 00:04:34,639
Yan is also very important to me.

85
00:04:35,439 --> 00:04:37,480
So you understand me, right?

86
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,279
How have you been lately?

87
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,480
You haven't had much rest either.

88
00:04:42,480 --> 00:04:43,600
As usual.

89
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,279
Do you have an answer?

90
00:04:45,759 --> 00:04:47,000
We are still amazing

91
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,759
at this pace.

92
00:04:49,319 --> 00:04:50,279
That's right.

93
00:04:50,439 --> 00:04:51,560
You can tell

94
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,759
that the two kids

95
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,720
have completely inherited from us.

96
00:05:22,199 --> 00:05:22,920
Yangyang,

97
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,040
why are you up so early?

98
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,040
Good morning, mom.

99
00:05:25,319 --> 00:05:26,240
Good morning.

100
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,959
Don't tell me you made this.

101
00:05:33,319 --> 00:05:34,160
I see how hard you work

102
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,800
getting up early to catch the bus every day,

103
00:05:36,279 --> 00:05:37,600
so I wanted to make you breakfast.

104
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:42,959
You know everything.

105
00:05:46,319 --> 00:05:47,639
So,

106
00:05:48,199 --> 00:05:49,480
you won't blame me, will you?

107
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:50,600
Of course not.

108
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:53,480
I just don't want you to be too tired.

109
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,519
Mom, can you promise me,

110
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,639
that if you're too busy

111
00:05:57,639 --> 00:05:58,879
or too tired,

112
00:05:59,199 --> 00:06:00,199
just don't come back.

113
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,160
I can take care of myself.

114
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:04,959
Okay.

115
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,439
I promise.

116
00:06:07,199 --> 00:06:08,560
Does that mean

117
00:06:08,959 --> 00:06:10,079
you also promise me

118
00:06:10,079 --> 00:06:11,759
I can go back and forth?

119
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,199
Thank you, son.

120
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:16,680
Thank you, mom.

121
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:24,480
Thank you.

122
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:27,439
You've worked hard.

123
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:28,920
It's okay.

124
00:06:29,759 --> 00:06:30,319
Sit down.

125
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:32,079
Come on.

126
00:06:32,879 --> 00:06:35,399
It's so beautiful.

127
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:37,920
Come on, mom.

128
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,079
Have a try.

129
00:06:40,759 --> 00:06:41,680
It's so exquisite.

130
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:42,879
I don't want to eat it.

131
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:44,839
It's okay.

132
00:06:44,839 --> 00:06:46,360
Just tell me how it is.

133
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,160
Okay.

134
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:56,759
Not bad.

135
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,120
You've got my touch.

136
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,360
Delicious.

137
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:01,720
Here.

138
00:07:02,639 --> 00:07:02,879
Okay.

139
00:07:02,879 --> 00:07:03,519
Thank you.

140
00:07:05,199 --> 00:07:06,000
You should eat too.

141
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:07,040
Go ahead.

142
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:08,160
Okay.

143
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,240
By the way, Mom,

144
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,959
on the road from Yibei to Fanghe,

145
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,040
there's a really beautiful flower field.

146
00:07:19,319 --> 00:07:20,279
Have you seen it?

147
00:07:20,279 --> 00:07:21,360
I know it.

148
00:07:21,639 --> 00:07:22,800
How do you know?

149
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,800
I even took pictures of it on my phone.

150
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,240
It's a secret.

151
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:30,439
Secret from me?

152
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:33,120
Next time I pass by

153
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:34,519
that sea of flowers,

154
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,560
I'll think of you.

155
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:39,839
Okay.

156
00:07:53,319 --> 00:07:53,680
Here you are.

157
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,519
Thank you, Uncle Zhang.

158
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,279
You're welcome.

159
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,399
Good morning, Uncle Zhang.

160
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:57,879
Yuan,

161
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,040
you're up early today.

162
00:07:59,040 --> 00:07:59,639
Yeah.

163
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:00,920
I'm about to

164
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,040
become a big brother.

165
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,680
I need to set a good example

166
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,560
for my little brother

167
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:05,959
or sister by going to bed

168
00:08:05,959 --> 00:08:06,639
and waking up early.

169
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,480
That's impressive.

170
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,480
I'm heading out.

171
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,639
Yuan,

172
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:11,319
um,

173
00:08:11,319 --> 00:08:12,319
where are your parents?

174
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,879
Still sleeping.

175
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,600
They never grow up.

176
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:19,399
You just received a big package.

177
00:08:19,399 --> 00:08:20,800
I called but no one answered.

178
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:21,240
So

179
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,279
I just left it here.

180
00:08:22,279 --> 00:08:23,639
Tell them

181
00:08:23,639 --> 00:08:24,800
to come pick it up

182
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,639
when they're free.

183
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:33,840
Uncle Zhang, forget it.

184
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,919
I'll carry them back myself.

185
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:36,200
They are on vacation recently,

186
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,679
and get up late in the afternoon.

187
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,320
They take up space here.

188
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,440
Can you do it with your small body?

189
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:42,279
Or I'll help you.

190
00:08:42,279 --> 00:08:43,000
No, no.

191
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,039
Your waist is not good.

192
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:45,080
You should rest more.

193
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,799
I play basketball.

194
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:47,960
This is a piece of cake

195
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:49,159
for me.

196
00:08:49,159 --> 00:08:49,720
Well,

197
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,759
take it easy.

198
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:52,799
I'm leaving, Uncle Zhang.

199
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:53,600
Be careful.

200
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,039
Okay.

201
00:08:54,039 --> 00:08:54,600
Bye.

202
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,320
What a big suitcase.

203
00:09:40,799 --> 00:09:42,279
Qingyuan, what's wrong with your arm?

204
00:09:42,559 --> 00:09:43,279
It's nothing.

205
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,360
Sports.

206
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,360
Love.

207
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,720
Call for

208
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,919
excellent photos.

209
00:10:28,919 --> 00:10:29,720
Sorry.

210
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,519
I dropped your bag.

211
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:32,279
It's okay.

212
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:34,200
What happened to your arm?

213
00:10:34,679 --> 00:10:36,279
I hurt it when I was moving stuff this morning.

214
00:10:36,519 --> 00:10:37,200
The doctor said

215
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,080
I've got a rotator cuff strain

216
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,440
in my right shoulder.

217
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:40,519
But it's okay.

218
00:10:41,679 --> 00:10:42,200
Then

219
00:10:42,879 --> 00:10:44,320
what about the competition next Saturday?

220
00:10:44,879 --> 00:10:45,840
Don't mention it.

221
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:46,919
I'm worrying about it.

222
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:50,120
Let me do it.

223
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,440
Just sit here.

224
00:10:52,879 --> 00:10:53,919
Well,

225
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:54,320
do you want to

226
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,559
enter the photography contest

227
00:10:55,559 --> 00:10:56,360
held by the magazine agency?

228
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,600
No.

229
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,039
Why?

230
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,480
Sports and Passion.

231
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,080
Isn't this

232
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,320
tailor-made for you?

233
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,159
The competition is more important.

234
00:11:05,159 --> 00:11:06,240
I can't be distracted.

235
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,919
Besides, you're injured.

236
00:11:09,639 --> 00:11:10,720
Let's keep things separate.

237
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,080
It's such a great opportunity.

238
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,960
If you really have no interest...

239
00:11:14,679 --> 00:11:15,720
It can be folded?

240
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,559
I accidentally folded it.

241
00:11:19,559 --> 00:11:20,440
Don't get the wrong idea.

242
00:11:20,759 --> 00:11:21,879
You're all talk and no action.

243
00:11:21,879 --> 00:11:23,279
You're holding the book upside down.

244
00:11:27,559 --> 00:11:29,039
Mind your own hands.

245
00:11:34,159 --> 00:11:34,519
Come on.

246
00:11:34,519 --> 00:11:35,120
I'll do it.

247
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:36,919
Thanks.

248
00:11:48,279 --> 00:11:50,480
What's this?

249
00:11:50,759 --> 00:11:51,600
Don't mention it.

250
00:11:51,879 --> 00:11:53,519
I hurt my right shoulder when moving things.

251
00:11:53,519 --> 00:11:55,399
Doctor said to hang it a week.

252
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:56,679
Then

253
00:11:56,679 --> 00:11:58,200
can you play in the next game?

254
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,080
Bro.

255
00:12:04,519 --> 00:12:06,120
Don't you become a substitute.

256
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,519
I can do it.

257
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,480
I'll be healed in time for the game.

258
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:10,399
No problem.

259
00:12:12,919 --> 00:12:14,200
Come over quickly.

260
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:15,679
I have something to tell you.

261
00:12:22,759 --> 00:12:23,519
Based on the data

262
00:12:23,519 --> 00:12:24,919
I've compiled,

263
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:26,919
I conclude that

264
00:12:28,159 --> 00:12:30,039
we need to increase our bench depth.

265
00:12:31,919 --> 00:12:33,399
Bench depth?

266
00:12:34,159 --> 00:12:34,960
Indeed.

267
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:36,399
The intensity of the game

268
00:12:36,399 --> 00:12:37,399
will be higher and higher.

269
00:12:38,159 --> 00:12:38,840
We can't just rely on

270
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,320
the starting five to carry the team.

271
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:42,559
Of course, they can't do it.

272
00:12:42,879 --> 00:12:44,440
So, starting from the next game,

273
00:12:44,519 --> 00:12:46,000
I plan to make one of the starting players

274
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,000
a substitute,

275
00:12:47,759 --> 00:12:48,919
also known as the sixth man.

276
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,399
First, rely on the four starters

277
00:12:50,399 --> 00:12:51,360
to open the situation.

278
00:12:51,679 --> 00:12:53,559
After the substitutes come on,

279
00:12:53,919 --> 00:12:54,840
we'll use the sixth man

280
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,000
to change the rhythm.

281
00:12:57,840 --> 00:12:58,720
That's feasible.

282
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:01,080
This person is nominally a substitute,

283
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:01,960
but in fact, he is also our

284
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:02,879
secret weapon.

285
00:13:03,799 --> 00:13:04,960
And in this way,

286
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,639
my choice of tactics with Coach Su

287
00:13:06,639 --> 00:13:07,919
can be more flexible.

288
00:13:08,559 --> 00:13:09,879
But we

289
00:13:10,639 --> 00:13:12,000
have to find a suitable substitute

290
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,720
after the starting lineup.

291
00:13:14,399 --> 00:13:15,360
Are there any suitable candidates

292
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:16,480
for the substitute?

293
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,559
For now,

294
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,240
Zhu Zhan is not bad.

295
00:13:23,879 --> 00:13:25,519
Is there anyone better at the perimeter?

296
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:26,559
Zhu Zhan

297
00:13:26,759 --> 00:13:28,120
is better at playing inside.

298
00:13:28,559 --> 00:13:29,440
I'm afraid

299
00:13:29,759 --> 00:13:31,080
he can't replace Lin Qingyuan.

300
00:13:31,759 --> 00:13:32,879
What are you talking about?

301
00:13:32,879 --> 00:13:33,799
I don't need to be replaced.

302
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:39,080
Then, for now,

303
00:13:39,799 --> 00:13:41,159
there's no suitable candidate.

304
00:14:11,879 --> 00:14:12,559
Wait.

305
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:15,080
I might have

306
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,480
an unexpected candidate.

307
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,440
Hello, Su.

308
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:33,440
Chen Song, have a seat.

309
00:14:35,559 --> 00:14:36,480
I've read

310
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:37,279
your script.

311
00:14:37,279 --> 00:14:38,919
It's fantastic,

312
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,559
especially the basketball parts.

313
00:14:40,559 --> 00:14:41,759
It really got me pumped.

314
00:14:41,759 --> 00:14:42,600
Really?

315
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:43,399
Thank you.

316
00:14:47,279 --> 00:14:48,080
What's up, Su?

317
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,399
Chen Song,

318
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:50,879
I've secretly looked into you.

319
00:14:50,879 --> 00:14:51,960
Looked into me?

320
00:14:52,399 --> 00:14:53,120
What did you find?

321
00:14:54,799 --> 00:14:55,960
Your basketball game report

322
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:57,320
is so professional.

323
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,159
There are many

324
00:14:58,159 --> 00:14:59,120
tactics in it

325
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:00,600
that I've never seen before.

326
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:01,919
Only after asking did I know

327
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,759
that you used to play basketball.

328
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,080
That's all in the past.

329
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,320
Tell me,

330
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,240
how did you play?

331
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,080
How long did you play?

332
00:15:12,720 --> 00:15:14,399
When I was five,

333
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,720
I was in a youth basketball team.

334
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,639
My dad said

335
00:15:18,639 --> 00:15:19,480
I wasn't growing tall,

336
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:21,120
so he wanted me to exercise more.

337
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:23,799
Give me the script.

338
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:24,960
Stand up.

339
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,480
Stand up.

340
00:15:27,159 --> 00:15:27,919
Back up.

341
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,159
A bit more.

342
00:15:31,559 --> 00:15:32,799
Show me how to dribble two balls.

343
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,960
Oh my.

344
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:44,360
So professional.

345
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,039
Not really.

346
00:15:46,039 --> 00:15:47,360
But I did learn

347
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,919
from professional coaches.

348
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,879
Until I finished primary school,

349
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,240
I found I prefer

350
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:53,360
writing alone,

351
00:15:53,799 --> 00:15:55,039
so I gave up.

352
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,639
Why didn't you tell us

353
00:15:56,639 --> 00:15:58,000
such an important thing?

354
00:15:58,600 --> 00:15:59,799
Is it important?

355
00:15:59,799 --> 00:16:01,080
Of course.

356
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:01,960
You played basketball

357
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,399
for five years.

358
00:16:03,399 --> 00:16:03,919
Maybe you're better

359
00:16:03,919 --> 00:16:04,679
than us.

360
00:16:04,679 --> 00:16:05,840
No, no, no.

361
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,799
I was always at the bottom of the class.

362
00:16:07,799 --> 00:16:10,120
I haven't played for a long time.

363
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:11,200
It doesn't matter.

364
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:11,960
Come on.

365
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,080
Go to apply for joining the Basketball Club

366
00:16:13,080 --> 00:16:14,200
with me now.

367
00:16:15,039 --> 00:16:15,799
No, no.

368
00:16:15,799 --> 00:16:16,639
I can't.

369
00:16:16,919 --> 00:16:19,000
I'm afraid of holding you back.

370
00:16:25,080 --> 00:16:25,759
Chen Song,

371
00:16:26,159 --> 00:16:26,840
don't you want to write

372
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:28,080
better works?

373
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:29,399
The most important thing

374
00:16:29,399 --> 00:16:31,159
in writing is to experience life.

375
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:32,799
Joining our basketball club

376
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,159
and playing more games

377
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:36,519
will surely inspire you.

378
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,399
Actually, I can learn by watching you.

379
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:39,279
It's the same.

380
00:16:39,279 --> 00:16:40,600
It's not the same.

381
00:16:40,919 --> 00:16:42,120
I've read scripts,

382
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,559
but does that mean I can write?

383
00:16:45,679 --> 00:16:47,000
Think about it.

384
00:16:47,279 --> 00:16:48,519
This is a big opportunity.

385
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,039
If you miss it,

386
00:16:50,039 --> 00:16:51,200
you might never get another.

387
00:16:57,120 --> 00:16:57,720
Fine.

388
00:16:58,039 --> 00:16:59,360
If you really don't want to

389
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,399
play with us,

390
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,600
then forget it.

391
00:17:01,799 --> 00:17:03,080
Let's just pretend

392
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:03,960
we never met.

393
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,839
You're still my good junior.

394
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:07,839
I'll still look out for you.

395
00:17:10,799 --> 00:17:11,960
I'm not sad at all.

396
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:12,880
See you.

397
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:37,920
Su.

398
00:17:44,799 --> 00:17:46,680
How about I give it a try?

399
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,400
That's what I'm waiting for.

400
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:49,079
Come on.

401
00:17:49,079 --> 00:17:49,839
Catch the ball.

402
00:18:15,440 --> 00:18:16,160
Nice!

403
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:18,079
Not bad, Chen Xiaosong.

404
00:18:18,359 --> 00:18:20,000
You're much better than I thought.

405
00:18:20,559 --> 00:18:21,599
Your basic skills are solid.

406
00:18:21,599 --> 00:18:22,400
It's clear you've

407
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:23,319
had professional training.

408
00:18:23,319 --> 00:18:24,599
Really,

409
00:18:24,839 --> 00:18:25,839
I still have a long way to go.

410
00:18:26,119 --> 00:18:27,519
I need to find my groove.

411
00:18:35,599 --> 00:18:36,480
Seniors,

412
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,359
what do you think?

413
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,599
Okay.

414
00:18:41,079 --> 00:18:41,640
I agree.

415
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,480
But you're from the junior high department.

416
00:18:43,799 --> 00:18:44,759
Coach Su and I

417
00:18:44,759 --> 00:18:45,839
will apply to Mr. Wang

418
00:18:46,480 --> 00:18:47,960
to let you join the club.

419
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,680
Wait.

420
00:18:49,279 --> 00:18:50,759
I have no objection to Chen Song joining the club.

421
00:18:51,519 --> 00:18:52,720
But

422
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,319
he won't take my place as a starter, will he?

423
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:57,720
We'll discuss this later.

424
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,720
You should focus on recovering.

425
00:18:58,720 --> 00:18:59,880
Don't worry about these.

426
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:00,640
No.

427
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:02,880
I have to make my attitude clear to you.

428
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,039
This game

429
00:19:04,039 --> 00:19:05,240
is very important to me.

430
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:06,720
I can't be on the bench.

431
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:07,279
Because after watching

432
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:08,440
this game,

433
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,000
your parents will go on a road trip.

434
00:19:10,599 --> 00:19:11,200
Yeah.

435
00:19:11,759 --> 00:19:12,759
They won't be able to watch

436
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:14,160
the rest of the games.

437
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,240
It's like a child's play.

438
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,839
According to Fu Binyan's analysis,

439
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,880
Xu Anbo is the one

440
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:22,920
with the most unstable condition.

441
00:19:23,839 --> 00:19:25,440
Can't he be the sixth man?

442
00:19:25,880 --> 00:19:27,079
I'm fine with it.

443
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,960
It's indeed rare to have a center

444
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,240
as the sixth man.

445
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,599
But in our case,

446
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,920
it's not gonna make much difference.

447
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,200
Anyway, my injury doesn't matter.

448
00:19:40,359 --> 00:19:40,720
What are you doing?

449
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:41,839
I'll prove it to you.

450
00:19:43,759 --> 00:19:44,160
Lin Qingyuan,

451
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,039
be careful.

452
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:52,720
Lin Qingyuan,

453
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,559
are you done?

454
00:19:55,759 --> 00:19:56,519
I'm not.

455
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,240
I was

456
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,000
forced to do it today,

457
00:20:01,839 --> 00:20:02,720
but

458
00:20:02,720 --> 00:20:03,359
I'm sure I'll be fine

459
00:20:03,359 --> 00:20:04,400
during the competition.

460
00:20:05,279 --> 00:20:06,160
Besides,

461
00:20:06,559 --> 00:20:08,680
you played with a wrist injury

462
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:10,160
before, didn't you?

463
00:20:14,480 --> 00:20:15,279
I can objectively assess

464
00:20:15,279 --> 00:20:16,480
my own injury.

465
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:17,480
Can you?

466
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,319
You just want to show off.

467
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,240
Why do you say that?

468
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:22,519
Gu Chenyang,

469
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,880
after all this time,

470
00:20:24,319 --> 00:20:25,559
you still look down on me.

471
00:20:29,519 --> 00:20:30,440
Say something.

472
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:31,519
Do you think

473
00:20:31,519 --> 00:20:32,640
Gu Chenyang is right?

474
00:20:39,759 --> 00:20:41,240
I'll do whatever the team decides.

475
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,440
I'll do whatever the team needs,

476
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:43,720
whether it's as a sub or a starter.

477
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:45,640
But please stop arguing.

478
00:20:46,599 --> 00:20:47,160
I...

479
00:20:47,519 --> 00:20:48,319
Me too.

480
00:20:54,279 --> 00:20:55,440
Alright,

481
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:57,279
let's not be so tense.

482
00:20:57,559 --> 00:20:59,279
We've got a new teammate here.

483
00:20:59,599 --> 00:21:00,359
Cheer up.

484
00:21:01,559 --> 00:21:02,880
I'll prove to you all

485
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,759
that I'm reliable.

486
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:07,519
Lin Qingyuan!

487
00:21:08,599 --> 00:21:09,559
Where are you going?

488
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:10,640
Lin Qingyuan!

489
00:21:22,759 --> 00:21:23,680
Keep practicing.

490
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,039
Take a break and recover these days.

491
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:56,359
Don't let it get to you.

492
00:23:01,720 --> 00:23:03,119
This guy is impressive!

493
00:23:03,119 --> 00:23:04,279
Even with a hand injury,

494
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,400
he's still giving it his all.

495
00:23:10,079 --> 00:23:11,000
Lin Qingyuan!

496
00:23:11,759 --> 00:23:12,359
Hello, principal.

497
00:23:12,359 --> 00:23:13,160
Remember to balance study and rest.

498
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:14,359
Do your best in the competition.

499
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,079
I'm looking forward to your good results.

500
00:23:16,359 --> 00:23:17,160
Thank you, principal.

501
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:17,720
Come on.

502
00:23:18,839 --> 00:23:19,400
Cheer up!

503
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,359
Cheer up!

504
00:24:05,519 --> 00:24:06,480
Cheer up!

505
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:20,839
Thank you.

506
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:46,759
He's been so cold to me these days.

507
00:24:46,759 --> 00:24:48,039
He's still mad at me.

508
00:24:48,519 --> 00:24:50,160
I told him to rest and recover,

509
00:24:50,759 --> 00:24:52,079
but he's training even harder.

510
00:24:53,559 --> 00:24:54,680
I saw it too.

511
00:24:55,279 --> 00:24:56,319
At this rate,

512
00:24:56,640 --> 00:24:58,160
he'll end up injuring himself.

513
00:25:03,119 --> 00:25:04,039
Bah, bah, bah.

514
00:25:04,680 --> 00:25:05,640
But why has he been

515
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:07,319
eating chicken wingtips lately?

516
00:25:10,079 --> 00:25:11,000
Does he think

517
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,359
wingtips can help

518
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:15,200
build up his shoulders?

519
00:25:16,559 --> 00:25:17,559
Definitely.

520
00:25:22,839 --> 00:25:23,599
Why is he

521
00:25:23,599 --> 00:25:24,839
so angry this time?

522
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:26,400
It doesn't make sense.

523
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:30,480
It's all because of you.

524
00:25:32,920 --> 00:25:33,720
Why?

525
00:25:37,759 --> 00:25:39,160
You bunch of idiots.

526
00:25:40,079 --> 00:25:40,720
You.

527
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:41,480
Come with me.

528
00:25:42,839 --> 00:25:43,599
I'll go first.

529
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,039
Okay, bye.

530
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:52,279
What's going on?
